Usage: agent-deck remove <id|title> [--force]

Remove a session by ID or title: kills its process, removes its
worktree and deletes it from the registry. A session that is still
running, waiting or idle with a live process is refused (exit 1)
unless --force is given, the same guard as 'session remove'.

Options:
  -force
    	Kill and remove a session that is still running/waiting/idle (destructive)
  -json
    	Output as JSON
  -q	Minimal output (short)
  -quiet
    	Minimal output

Examples:
  agent-deck remove abc12345
  agent-deck remove "My Project" --force   # also when it is running
  agent-deck -p work remove abc12345   # Remove from 'work' profile
